  "what_happened_next": {
    "text": "IBM more than tripled, leading these choices after a difficult early stretch. Ford, Disney and the US basket also more than doubled. A famous company could struggle and recover, but a recovery was never guaranteed. This result should not turn every troubled company into an automatic bargain.\n\nDuring the period, astronauts repaired Hubble, South Africa held its first national democratic election open to all races, and Windows 95 reached shops. Changes in science, politics and everyday technology continued while people held their investments. These events explain the setting, but they do not pin each rise or fall in a share price to one cause.\n\nLook at IBM’s difficult months before its recovery. Would you have stayed with your original choice? The game lets you see the whole route at once; an investor then received only the next piece of news. A low price can reflect a genuine problem as well as a possible opportunity, so a later recovery should not be treated as inevitable.",
    "source_ids": [
